    "narrative": "For the May 21st slate, the Austin Waves offense is anchored by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who carries our highest efficiency score of 78.53. Despite facing Rod\u00f3n, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains a mandatory start due to an excellent 0.376 xwOBA and a favorable dynamic platoon advantage that boosts his projection significantly. Behind him, **Josh Lowe** (70.14) is our secondary standout; his aggressive deployment against Severino, L is bolstered by a +14% boost from his dynamic platoon split, making him the premier source of speed and power for today\u2019s lineup. While **Nolan Schanuel** (59.81) and **Dominic Smith** (53.85) provide solid, albeit unspectacular, production against mid-tier arms like Severino, L and Alcantara, S, their favorable lineup positions and stable expected ERAs keep them safely in the active slot over more volatile options.\n\nManaging our limited starts remains the primary driver of today\u2019s bench decisions. **Nasim Nunez** (49.48) narrowly edged out fringe bench contributors, despite a -6% penalty for hitting in the #8 spot and a slight downgrade for facing a lefty in Peterson, D. We are keeping a close watch on **Liam Hicks** (52.47), whose start against Strider presents the most significant risk of the day; while his dynamic platoon advantage against a righty keeps him above the 50-point threshold, Strider\u2019s raw stuff always carries the potential to deflate offensive output despite the 4.20 xERA. With **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Jackson Merrill** all inactive due to scheduled off-days and **Luis Robert Jr.** remaining sidelined on the IL, our roster depth is currently tested, placing the onus on **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Josh Lowe** to carry the weight of our 5x5 category production today.",
